Package: metabeta
Type: Package
Title: Amortized Bayesian Mixed Models with a 'brms' Interface
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alex", "Kipnis", email = "adkipnis@mailbox.org", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Marcel", "Binz", email = "marcel.binz@tuebingen.mpg.de", role = "aut"))
Description: A drop-in replacement for the user interface of 'brms'
    (brm(), summary(), fixef(), ranef(), posterior_predict(), loo(), ...)
    that fits generalized linear mixed models with the pretrained amortized
    posterior estimator 'metabeta' instead of Stan. Gaussian, Bernoulli and
    Poisson models with one grouping factor are supported. Posterior draws are
    refined by independence Metropolis-Hastings chains that use the learned
    normalizing flow as their proposal, so the delivered posterior targets the
    exact model while typically taking well under a second.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
URL: https://github.com/adkipnis/metabeta
BugReports: https://github.com/adkipnis/metabeta/issues
